        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-27T20:38:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, it\u0027s definitely a good assert. I was semi-concerned about the cost of doing lots of redundant memory writes, since my expectation is either a given runtime effect is used once (in which case find+set doesn\u0027t amount to much vs. set-only) or we see the effect a lot (in which case many finds + 1 set could be faster than many sets?).\n\nWould be nice if there were an addIfNotExists() or if we had APIs like the new Node-based ones that let find return pointers to the internal data structures so you can do sets after the fact if you\u0027d want.  But I\u0027m pre-emptively optimizing, so lets leave it as this.",
